# The port's half of the mu- like-for-like. Run it with examples/B1/exampleB1.exe; its partner
# is muon_emonly.mac, run with ref/run/runb1.bat against the real Geant4 build of B1.
#
# No /process/inactivate lines, because there is nothing here to inactivate: this port gives a
# muon Transportation, multiple scattering and continuous ionisation and nothing else, which is
# what muon_emonly.mac reduces QBBC to. (The port's G4UImanager reports an unknown command
# rather than ignoring it, so the two files cannot be the same file.)
#
# MEASURED, 20,000 events each, six random seeds on the Geant4 side and the printed rms on this
# one:
#
#   mu-   port 23.8091 +/- 0.126 nGy   Geant4 23.0992 +/- 0.037   +3.07%, 5.4 sigma
#   mu+   port 23.8629 +/- 0.127 nGy   Geant4 23.9259 +/- 0.056   -0.26%, 0.45 sigma
#
# So mu+ agrees and mu- does not, and the two numbers together are the finding rather than
# either alone. Geant4's own mu+ minus mu- is 0.827 +/- 0.067 nGy - 3.58% at 12 sigma, and 3.94%
# with nothing inactivated at all - while its own restricted dE/dx and range tables for the two
# differ by 0.23% and 0.30% (ref/oracle/hadron_tables.csv, G4_WATER at 199.526 MeV). The port
# reproduces THOSE to 0.05% and separates its two muons by 0.24%. A dose asymmetry fifteen
# times larger than the stopping-power asymmetry that is supposed to cause it is not in the
# tables, and what is left charge-odd in a 200 MeV mu- once ionisation is excluded is multiple
# scattering - G4MuMultipleScattering with G4WentzelVIModel, whose single-scattering tail runs
# through G4WentzelOKandVIxSection. Open; see docs/RISK.md V38.
#
# MSC IS EXCLUDED, AND IT IS NOT THE MUON'S. Re-measured at 500,000 events per beam, with the
# pion and the kaon beside it:
#
#   mu-   port 597.326 +/- 0.633 nGy   Geant4 575.568 +/- 0.611   +3.78%, 24.7 sigma
#   mu+   port 598.660 +/- 0.634 nGy   Geant4 600.681 +/- 0.634   -0.34%,  2.25 sigma
#   pi-   port 630.922 +/- 0.666        Geant4 600.831 +/- 0.636   +5.01%, 32.7 sigma
#   pi+   port 632.349 +/- 0.668        Geant4 633.446 +/- 0.668   -0.17%,  1.16 sigma
#   kaon- port 1239.62 +/- 1.303        Geant4 1131.87 +/- 1.195   +9.52%, 61.0 sigma
#   kaon+ port 1242.97 +/- 1.306        Geant4 1240.74 +/- 1.302   +0.18%,  1.21 sigma
#
# Inactivating msc on the Geant4 side moves the muon split from 4.36% to 3.99% and the pion's
# from 5.43% to 5.35% - see pion_nomsc.mac, which also records how the inactivations were
# verified. And the split vanishes at 1 GeV (pion_1gev.mac) and orders by mass at fixed kinetic
# energy, which is by 1/beta. So it is neither multiple scattering nor a muon peculiarity: it is
# a low-velocity, charge-odd effect common to every negative hadron. docs/RISK.md carries what
# is excluded and what is left.
#
# CLOSED - docs/RISK.md V46. All six re-run at 500,000 events with the fix in; this file is the
# mu- row. The three POSITIVES are bit-identical to the numbers above, which is what says the
# fix selected the negatives rather than rescaling everything:
#
#                    port BEFORE         port AFTER          Geant4 EM-only      after
#   mu-    597.326 +/- 0.633   575.145 +/- 0.611   575.568 +/- 0.611   -0.073%, 0.49 sigma
#   mu+    598.660 +/- 0.634   598.660 +/- 0.634   600.681 +/- 0.634   -0.34%,  2.25 sigma
#   pi-    630.922 +/- 0.666   600.871 +/- 0.636   600.831 +/- 0.636   +0.007%, 0.04 sigma
#   pi+    632.349 +/- 0.668   632.349 +/- 0.668   633.446 +/- 0.668   -0.17%,  1.16 sigma
#   kaon-  1239.62 +/- 1.303   1132.65 +/- 1.199   1131.87 +/- 1.195   +0.069%, 0.46 sigma
#   kaon+  1242.97 +/- 1.306   1242.97 +/- 1.306   1240.74 +/- 1.302   +0.18%,  1.21 sigma
#
# 24.7, 32.7 and 61.0 sigma became 0.49, 0.04 and 0.46. The port's own charge splits are now
# 4.09%, 5.24% and 9.74% against Geant4's 4.36%, 5.43% and 9.62%.
#
# WHAT IT WAS, and it is not in this file's list of suspects because it is not a PROCESS.
# G4VEnergyLossProcess::AlongStepDoIt takes its long-step branch on every step here - a 200 MeV
# hadron loses ~5% of its energy per step and linLossLimit is 0.01 - so the continuous loss is
# a difference of two RANGE-table lookups and never touches the dE/dx table these headers kept
# comparing. Geant4 interpolates that range table LINEARLY for the second-registered member of
# every charge pair, because G4EmBuilder registers one shared G4hBremsstrahlung between the two
# and G4MuBremsstrahlung's constructor calls SetSpline(false). Five source lines, in V46.
#
# 200 MeV: a mu- range of 861 mm in water against B1's ~360 mm of world, so nothing stops and
# this is a plateau dose. Confirmed rather than assumed - the Geant4 run with
# muMinusCaptureAtRest left ACTIVE gives a bit-identical 22.9917 nGy, so no muon reached rest.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/gun/particle mu-
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn 500000
